\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The full metric-class table, with the within-correct column.} Prediction-fit and weighted-similarity metrics rank on hard benchmarks and their saturated point estimates collapse or turn negative; raw overlap does not rank at all (its hard-benchmark inversion is a verbosity confound: controlling output length moves $-0.49$ to $-0.07$). Human columns are Pearson $r$ with bootstrap 95\% CIs on the 60-item set; gold-token logprob uses the $n{=}42$ subset with logprob available; the within-correct column is from the canonical analysis (\texttt  {canonical\_validity.json}), with $n{=}48$ for every signal except gold-token logprob ($n{=}32$); the best full-set human-anchored value is in bold. The within-correct column shows that no cheap signal, comparison or verification, demonstrably grades beyond correctness on this anchor set: \textsc  {TFA}'s $+0.21$ ($n{=}48$, interval wide) ties or exceeds every verification signal's within-correct value. The referenced judge's $-0.14$ reflects range restriction on the random set; the same judge reads $+0.81$ within-correct on the divergence-selected stratum of the companion audit~\cite  {companionA}, and is the only signal shown to grade beyond correctness. \textbf  {Takeaway:} on the full set no comparison metric grades and the deeper verification signals do, while on the within-correct margin nothing cheap is separable from noise.}}{12}{table.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:classfull}{{3}{12}{\textbf {The full metric-class table, with the within-correct column.} Prediction-fit and weighted-similarity metrics rank on hard benchmarks and their saturated point estimates collapse or turn negative; raw overlap does not rank at all (its hard-benchmark inversion is a verbosity confound: controlling output length moves $-0.49$ to $-0.07$). Human columns are Pearson $r$ with bootstrap 95\% CIs on the 60-item set; gold-token logprob uses the $n{=}42$ subset with logprob available; the within-correct column is from the canonical analysis (\texttt {canonical\_validity.json}), with $n{=}48$ for every signal except gold-token logprob ($n{=}32$); the best full-set human-anchored value is in bold. The within-correct column shows that no cheap signal, comparison or verification, demonstrably grades beyond correctness on this anchor set: \tfa 's $+0.21$ ($n{=}48$, interval wide) ties or exceeds every verification signal's within-correct value. The referenced judge's $-0.14$ reflects range restriction on the random set; the same judge reads $+0.81$ within-correct on the divergence-selected stratum of the companion audit~\cite {companionA}, and is the only signal shown to grade beyond correctness. \textbf {Takeaway:} on the full set no comparison metric grades and the deeper verification signals do, while on the within-correct margin nothing cheap is separable from noise}{table.caption.12}{}}
